The attached image (Figure 7D) is a Western blot that verifies the presence of active IL-1β (17 kD) in the supernatant of bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) treated with Nano-11, particularly after LPS priming. It shows that LPS alone induces pro-IL-1β (31 kD) in cell lysates but not secreted active IL-1β. Nano-11 alone induces a small amount of active IL-1β secretion. However, when BMDCs are primed with LPS and then stimulated with Nano-11, there is a substantial increase in the secretion of the active 17 kD IL-1β in the supernatant, confirming Nano-11's role in promoting IL-1β cleavage and secretion, a critical pro-inflammatory cytokine in immune activation.